]
]  Hello fellow Net-Hackers!
]	I just got ver 2.3 from Grape and am having a little trouble
]getting it to run.  No matter what I do Nethack always tells me that
]it doesn't know my assigned value for TERM.  I must have tried a
]million times to get it to work, but it just doesn't seem to want
]to go.  Maybe I'm missing something stupid, but version 2.2 works
]just fine.  I'm hoping someone out there will be able to enlighten me.

First, you have to
set TERM=nansi-color
at the DOS prompt.  (Replace nansi-color with something appropriate for 
your system.)
Then, be sure you have the file termcap.cnf in your path somewhere.
What's that?  You don't know what's appropriate or have termcap.cnf?
OK, download the file nhacksup.arc from grape.

That should do it; I haven't had any trouble with the new version.  Of
course, I only played one level; I am really busy with school right now.


